## When to use — and when not to **[core]**

| Use this rule | Use something else |
|---------------|-------------------|
| UI beauty pass without feature creep | Mode A |
| Open-ended business idea → Jobs-style vision | Mode C |
| Rapid structured ideation tables | Mode B |
| Feature overload, scope cut, "what to remove" | Mode C or `product-council.mdc` |
| Go/no-go, CIRCLES, engineer/QA/security lenses | `product-council.mdc` |
| Ruthless **task** backlog triage (not product scope) | outside this rule |
| Time-critical call with no room for reflection | decide first; council later |

**Disambiguation:** `focus` on **tasks/time** → not this rule | `focus` on **product scope** → this rule or council | `prioritize features` → Mode C essentialism or council **Cut** step.

